.TH SDL_strrev 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_strrev \- Reverse a string\(aqs contents.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "char * SDL_strrev(char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This reverses a null-terminated string in-place\[char46] Only the content of the string is reversed; the null-terminator character remains at the end of the reversed string\[char46]
.PP
.BR WARNING :
This function reverses the _bytes_ of the string, not the codepoints\[char46] If
.BR str
is a UTF-8 string with Unicode codepoints > 127, this will ruin the string data\[char46] You should only use this function on strings that are completely comprised of low ASCII characters\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I str
the string to reverse\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR str \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

